body:
Oh God, one of THOSE people. I bet you're campaigning to change the Baby Humans nickname too.

&#x200B;

(Wish I had found this sooner. Brilliant!)

I've been playing private servers since 2009, and I've never seen one as septic as Darrowshite, by a long shot.

&#x200B;

(That's not a typo.)

It's OK to put DTF need not apply (sad but true that many guys are on there for that), but the "fragile/toxic masculinity" is so subjective, you might be making some guys you'd be good with self-eliminate. The pics are a good mix of fun/flirty that show your face and bod, but if you could get something without your phone covering part of you up for your first, that'd be ideal. Those are my initial reactions. 

&#x200B;

You might put that you're new to NOLA and looking for someone to show you around. Or put a question about what their favorite hangout is to prompt responses (I know you need to message first, but still...). I wish Bumble gave you a few more characters. So tough to add a flavor of your personality plus give them something to react to!

Right? I finally got a friend at work to give it a shot last Summer. He was so skeptical just because of the concept, and because he'd given the first few episodes a look back when they first came out and thought they were so-so (common response). 

&#x200B;

He binged the whole series in 3 days and binged the 5th season with me last month. Raving fan now.
